<!-- HERO -->
<section style="position:relative;min-height:560px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;overflow:hidden;">
  <img src="/images/hero-panorama.webp" alt="Perth landscape" width="2000" height="950" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
  <div style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(10,61,92,0.55) 0%, rgba(10,61,92,0.25) 55%, rgba(10,61,92,0.45) 100%);"></div>
  <div style="position:relative;max-width:880px;padding:96px 24px 130px;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:18px;padding:7px 18px;border-radius:10px;font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.14);color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.35);backdrop-filter:blur(3px);">Walls · Cracks · Patios · Perth</span>
    <h1 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-weight:800;color:#fff;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.015em;font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,58px);margin:0 0 18px;text-shadow:0 2px 24px rgba(10,61,92,0.45);">Structural Engineering in Perth: Load Bearing Wall Removal, Cracks and Extensions</h1>
    <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.92);max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 30px;text-shadow:0 1px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.5);">Kings Park Structural Co is a referral service for home owners across Greater Perth, the Perth Hills and Peel, paid by the independent structural engineering firm that advertises here. Call or send photos and plans, and that firm's engineer looks at your wall, crack, extension or patio and quotes you directly.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <a href="tel:+61855506237" class="btn-green" style="font-size:15px;padding:16px 38px;">Call Now — (08) 5550 6237</a>
      <a href="/#contact" class="btn-white-outline" style="font-size:15px;">Get a Written Quote</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <svg class="swoosh" style="position:absolute;bottom:0;left:0;" viewBox="0 0 1440 70" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0,70 C360,10 1080,10 1440,70 L1440,70 L0,70 Z" fill="#ffffff"/></svg>
</section>

<!-- INTRO -->
<section style="padding:84px 24px 64px;background:#fff;">
  <div class="intro-grid" style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.9fr 1.1fr;gap:64px;align-items:center;">
    <div style="position:relative;">
      <div style="border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 24px 56px rgba(10,61,92,0.22);aspect-ratio:1/1;">
        <img src="/images/about.webp" alt="Kings Park Structural Co service crew" width="1024" height="1024" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      <div style="position:absolute;bottom:-18px;right:-14px;background:#1F5E8C;color:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:14px 22px;box-shadow:0 10px 26px rgba(47,163,77,0.4);">
        <p style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;margin:0;line-height:1;">Perth-wide</p>
        <p style="font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;margin:4px 0 0;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;">Independent structural engineers quote your job</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">Perth houses, brick and sand</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 18px;">Most Perth homes are brick, and that changes which walls can come out</h2>
      <div class="rich"><p>Load bearing wall removal in Perth is the job most people ring about, and there's a reason for it. WA is the only state where more than half of detached houses are brick, at 68 per cent, and in a double-brick house some internal walls usually carry the ceiling and roof as well as the external walls. Removing a wall that supports anything else falls outside the building permit exemption, so the engineer's beam design goes in with the permit application. Start with <a href="/blog/how-to-tell-if-a-wall-is-load-bearing/">the clues you can check yourself</a>, then read how <a href="/wall-removal-engineering/">wall removal engineering</a> works.</p><p>Kings Park Structural Co is a referral service, not an engineering firm. We pass your enquiry to an independent structural engineering firm, which pays to advertise here and quotes and contracts with you directly. From 1 July 2027, structural engineering work in WA must be done by a registered building engineer, and you can check anyone on the DEMIRS Building Engineer Register. Engineers quote each job, so <a href="/structural-engineer-cost-perth/">our cost guide</a> explains what drives the price instead of inventing one.</p></div>
      <a href="/about/" class="btn-blue" style="margin-top:10px;">More About Us</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .intro-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; gap: 44px !important; } }
</style>

<!-- TILES -->
<section id="services" style="padding:72px 24px 84px;background:#F1ECE2;">
  <div style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
    <span class="kicker">Where people usually start</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 40px;">Is that wall holding something up, or is that crack telling you something?</h2>
    <div class="tile-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:22px;">
      <a href="/wall-removal-engineering/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-1.webp" alt="Internal brick wall between a kitchen and lounge in a Perth home, marked out for removal" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Removing a load-bearing wall</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/structural-inspections/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-2.webp" alt="Diagonal crack running from the corner of a window in a rendered Perth wall" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Cracks in walls, ceilings or brickwork</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/extension-engineering/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-3.webp" alt="Timber frame of a second-storey addition going up on a single-storey brick house" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Second storey or extension</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/patio-shed-certificates/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-4.webp" alt="Colorbond patio roof on steel posts over a backyard alfresco area" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Patio, carport or shed certificate</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/steel-beam-for-wall-removal/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-1.webp" alt="Steel beam spanning an opening where an internal wall was removed" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Steel beam for an open-plan kitchen</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/cracks-in-brick-walls/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-2.webp" alt="Step crack following the mortar joints in a face brick wall" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Step cracks in brick walls</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/rusted-lintels-perth/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-3.webp" alt="Cracked brickwork above a window where a steel lintel has rusted" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Rusted lintels above windows</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/cracks-in-concrete-slab/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-4.webp" alt="Crack across a concrete floor slab with the floor covering lifted" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;padding:14px 12px;">Cracked concrete slab</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
